t we traverse the boundary once in the counterclockwise direction starting from the origin.\n\n![](images/23/231dd5f96cd36d21940fcee894382edc9eabc91b0bf72bb4a8724c8444f76a8c.png)\n\nLet the affine transformation $\\mathbf T$ be defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & ={{[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ -1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo find the image of $\\Delta$ under the action of $\\mathbf T,$ we set up the following matrices:\n\n- The matrix $U$ containing all vertices of our triangle, presented in the order shown in the diagram:\n![](images/34/34be6d7cd24938fb72976910cf3ad6a790eb93574915829f621da99f4aec3838.svg)\n\n- The matrix $B$ that has the same shape as $U$ and with the vector $\\mathbf b$ in each column:\n![](images/be/bed30fcc6a1003bee7f2f7888af9c301314b2aba351497db35cf2ee37710c0a1.svg)\n\nThe image of $\\mathbf u$ under $T$ is given by $A\\mathbf u + \\mathbf b.$ So, by applying $\\mathbf T$ to $U,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}AU+B & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 \\\\ 1 & 0\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 & 1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -1 & -1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 1 & 2 \\\\ -1 & 0 & -1\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe vertices of the image are given by the columns of the above matrix. Drawing these vertices in the order shown, i.e.\n\n$$\n(1,-1) \\to (1,0) \\to (2,-1),\n$$\n\nwe get the following picture:\n\n![](images/d5/d514834e6e9f108f478002416e863cf9c98d00add230c2e9321664ea14e5db0e.png)\n\n          \n\nNotice that the polygon $D$ is traversed in the *clockwise* direction." 13194139534292 17592186045417 true] [17592186180755 1064 "Consider the triangle $\\Delta$ with sides $S_1, S_2,$ and 