 #edb/ref 17592186045493 13194139534292 17592186045417 true] [17592186417835 1077 "selection" 13194139534292 17592186045417 true] [17592186417835 1078 #edb/ref 17592186417827 13194139534292 17592186045417 true] [17592186417835 1079 #uuid "cc6bf158-bc5a-5b83-aecb-e172b7a9b66e" 13194139534292 17592186045417 true] [17592186417836 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417834 13194139534292 17592186045417 true] [17592186417836 1069 "q-124153" 13194139534292 17592186045417 true] [17592186417836 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534292 17592186045417 true] [17592186417836 1071 "Consider the transformation $T$ defined as\n\n$$\nx=4u+v-1,\\,y=-u-3v+1.\n$$\n\nLet $P(-3,1)$ be a point in the $uv$-plane. Suppose that the image of $P$ under the action of $T$ is the point ${P}^{′}$ in the $xy$-plane. What are the coordinates of ${P}^{′}?$" 13194139534292 17592186045417 true] [17592186417836 1072 #uuid "6cb153c3-10ae-52e4-a409-49d1a1150376" 13194139534292 17592186045417 true] [17592186417836 1074 "An affine transformation $T:{R}^{2}\\to {R}^{2}$ is a function of the form\n\n$$\nx=Au+b,\n$$\n\nwhere $x,u,$ and $b$ are column vectors in ${R}^{2},$ and $A$ is a $2\\times 2$ matrix.\n\nNotice that the given transformation can be expressed as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}4u+v-1 \\\\ -u-3v+1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & =[\\begin{aligned}4u+v \\\\ -u-3v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\  & ={{[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{A}\\cdot {{[\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{u}+{{[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]}_{⏟}}_{b}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, to find the image of $P$ under the action of $T,$ we first create a column vector $u$ containing the coordinates of $P:$ \n\n$$\nu=[\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nApplying $T$ to $u,$ we get\n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}4 & 1 \\\\ -1 & -3\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}-3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}-1 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}-12 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of ${P}^{′}$ are $(-12,1).$" 13194139534292 17592186045417 true] [17592186417837 1068 #edb/ref 17592186417835 13194139534292 17592186045417 true] [17592186417837 1069 "q-162181" 13194139534292 17592186045417 true] [17592186417837 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 13194139534292 17592186045417 true] [17592186417837 1071 "Consider the affine transformation $T,$ defined as\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}[\\begin{aligned}x \\\\ y\\end{aligned}] & =[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}]\\cdot [\\begin{aligned}u \\\\ v\\end{aligned}]+[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWhat is the area scale factor of the transformation?" 13194139534292 17592186045417 true] [17592186417837 1072 #uuid "914af94d-7042-54e6-acb1-fed694c9a4de" 13194139534292 17592186045417 true] [17592186417837 1074 "The matrix representation of the linear transformation associated with $T$ is $A=[\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}].$ \n\nComputing the determinant of $A,$ we get\n\n$$\ndet(A)=|\\begin{aligned}1 & 2 \\\\ 3 & 4\\end{aligned}|=1\\cdot 4-3\\cdot 2=-2.\n$$\n\nSo, the area scale factor of the transformation is\n\n$$\n|det(A)|=|-2|=2.\n$$" 13194139534292 17592186045417 true]] :edb/tempids {"answer-0bc4fab2-f286-5943-a45f-a20492b01ffd" 17592186417824 "answer-15292884-dc42-57e9-9c54-15240ddfccc9" 17592186417825 "answer-73315599-47f7-5acb-b194-b9be8f07b4fe" 17592186417826 "answer-76b47f26-b551-5ab2-a16b-a5772ef735ad" 17592186417827 "answer-79732bdc-fd7e-5901-92b4-c5585d62e3b9" 17592186417828 "answer-94a311b2-4197-58fb-9f74-f9df05de251a" 17592186417829 "answer-99809079-4b95-5960-860d-5696a69fc28e" 17592186417830 "answer-ca24dbee-3bf2-5067-b768-9753b1ef80ef" 17592186417831 "answer-d2847d2c-57b6-59e8-b9ce-cd6f7d5c8fab" 17592186417832 "answer-f0b0cc75-4660-5f89-b375-205d3cc92d47" 17592186417833 "answer-field-69877276-8edf-5389-b9b6-59ddab5b630a" 17592186417834 "answer-field-cc6bf15